modem73 is Unlicense software by RFnexus:
https://github.com/RFnexus/modem73

Windows binaries come from the experimental Win32 port:
https://github.com/RFnexus/modem73-win

Release archives include the upstream binary as-is so a station can be
installed with no extra download. That binary is not Apache-2.0.
macOS archives also include the `libs/` folder (`@executable_path/libs`).
See the Unlicense at the upstream repository, and MODEM73-LICENSE in the
release zip when present.

`wcr` downloads a missing modem73 from its **own** WeeChat Radio release
tag, never from `/releases/latest`. The release workflow hashes the modem73
asset it bundles and builds that SHA-256 into `wcr` (`WCR_MODEM73_SHA256`),
so the download always matches the bundled copy. Builds made outside the
release workflow fall back to release `v0.1.79` and the hashes in
`sha256.json` next to this file.
